{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Whoever is simple</b> — you do not call them thus, rather they are called by the name of their end, or you call them by such a name to exaggerate the deficiency of their awareness, because of the intensity of the pleasure and gratification that come to them with her, and because she was compelled to call them, while they did not know her worth."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:46.507615805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}